From 120f7da469206864c320a7212d5cf7fedb38705e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heresy <heresy@local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:05:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1021/1198] Stems on Forge and the tree of what is made from a
 take

HERESY 1021.
- Post has Stems: heresy-lab splits a take with BS-Roformer ep317 (vocals,
  instrumental; SDR 12.97 on vocals) and optionally htdemucs_ft on the
  instrumental (drums, bass, other), FLAC 24-bit at 48 kHz, ~4 and ~6 minutes
  for a 7-minute take on a 3090. Weights live in the Kit (separation/), the
  lab has its own venv (torch, audio-separator, faster-whisper): nothing
  outside the Kit is used.
- Everything made from a take goes into outputs/TAKE/derived/ID/ with a
  manifest, shown in Post as a tree under the take: each file plays, can be
  laid over the take in the spectrum, and a vocal stem can be given to the
  lyrics check (which now has a source choice).
- The Kit server passes Range through /lab/ (the players seek) and writes
  with a 60 s timeout instead of 5: two big answers sharing a phone line cut
  one of them. The spectrum asks Forge again on a dropped transfer and no
  longer falls back to downloading the whole file while the lab is alive.
- The full-screen spectrum zooms up to 4K wide and no further.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
